{
  "assembly": {
    "id": "driveline-haldex",
    "name": "Drivetrain — 4MOTION (Haldex Gen 5)",
    "system": "drivetrain",
    "origin": [
      0,
      0,
      0
    ],
    "description": "The AWD path (dossier §4): the gearbox's bevel box sends torque down a two-piece propshaft to the rear final drive, where the Haldex Gen 5 electro-hydraulic coupling sits AHEAD of the rear differential — pre-emptively clutching up to ~50% of torque rearward before slip happens. Plus the front and rear driveshafts with their CV joints. The coupling's pump and fine-mesh filter are the famous service item: they clog on hard-driven cars and fail with no dash warning."
  },
